      "source": "research/physics-remaining-80-2026-10-17-alpha-batch-26-3a.md",
      "Omega": "(e,infinity) with Lebesgue measure",
      "parameters": "beta=k=T=1",
      "H": "log x + 2 log log x",
      "Z": 1,
      "q": "1/[x (log x)^2]",
      "independent_verification": "Put t=log x: q dm=dt/t^2 on (1,infinity), whose total integral is 1. H=t+2log t>=t, so Gibbs energy diverges as integral dt/t. Since log q=-H, integral |q log q| also diverges. Uniform p on (e,e+1) has p=1 there, zero entropy and finite bounded energy. For R>e, q-conditioned (e,R) has c_R=1-1/log R and D=-log c_R tending to zero, so finite-functional infimum F=0 has no minimizer."
    }
  },
